Subject: Select register-independent native animation rotation decoders

Upstream-base: 4a9ab8151d9a74e321e52b36c95d1e157d41af60

Keep the console GQR setup and paired-single assembly in the console branch.
On native builds the port supplies scalar rotation decoding with the same
signed formats, fixed GQR scale factors and original twelve-bit packing.
Compile the original unsigned scale and byte-weight implementations unchanged.
Document the packed-byte versus host-order structure contract explicitly;
this does not convert animation chunks, relocate pointers, or blend poses.

diff --git a/include/Game/SAnimDecode.h b/include/Game/SAnimDecode.h
index 7df4c80..0361edb 100644
--- a/include/Game/SAnimDecode.h
+++ b/include/Game/SAnimDecode.h
@@ -5,6 +5,14 @@
 
 struct PackedScale;
 
+#ifdef MSCHARGED_NATIVE
+// Rotation inputs remain packed big-endian bytes (8/6/4 bytes respectively),
+// including unaligned keys. Outputs are host-order floats, without normalization.
+// PackedScale is an aligned host-order struct of three unsigned 16-bit fields;
+// its asset loader must convert Wii byte order before calling the decoder.
+// Weight inputs are single unsigned bytes. Input/output storage must not overlap.
+// Scalar rotation decoders encode the original GQR constants and need no state.
+#endif
 void SAnimInitGQR();
 extern "C" void SAnimDecodeRot16(nlQuaternion* result, const void* packed);
 extern "C" void SAnimDecodeRot12(nlQuaternion* result, const void* packed);
